          '`src/world/kit/lights.js` exports `buildLights(manifest, ctx, placement)` returning `{ ids, group }`: each `room.lights` entry is registered with `ctx.lightManager.registerLight({ id: <building>:<lightId>, x, y, z (world, converted with the placement and the room floor y), color, intensity, distance, group, room: <roomId>, auto, emissive: [bulb] })` where `bulb` is a sphere of radius 0.08 in `emissiveWarm` placed at the light position inside `group` (the interior group). `src/world/kit/lifts.js` exports `buildLifts(manifest, ctx, placement)` returning `{ lifts, group }`: manifest lifts have `floors` as LEVEL INDICES (plan 020 schema); map them to `y = manifest.floors[level].y` (building y plus placement y) and call `createLift({ id: <building>:<liftId>, x, z, width, depth, rot, floors: [y...], world, registry, events })` (x, z, rot converted with the placement); `createLift` (plan 018) owns the cabin floor collider, the shaft back and side colliders and the door colliders; this module only adds meshes: shaft walls (`metalPainted`, boxes 0.08 thick around the cabin on three sides from the lowest floor y to the highest floor y + 2.6), a door frame per floor on the entrance side (`metalBrushed`, 1.1 m wide, 2.2 m high), two door leaf boxes per floor that are visible except while `lift.state === "open"` at that floor, and a cabin box (floor slab, ceiling slab, back wall) that follows `lift.y` each `update`. The lift id prefix makes plan 018 name the interactables `<building>:<liftId>-call-<n>` and `<building>:<liftId>-btn-<n>`. Every door and lift is also pushed into `ctx.doorList` / `ctx.liftList` when those arrays exist (the game loop updates them, plans 017 and 018).',
          'Test fixtures (new files; the 020 originals stay untouched): `tests/fixtures/manifests/cottageFull.json` = a copy of `cottage.json` plus: `lights` `{ id: "hall-1", x, y: 2.6, z, color: "#ffd9a0", intensity: 18, distance: 10, group: "hall" }` in `hall` (no `auto`) and `{ id: "bed-1", ..., group: "bedroom" }` in `bedroom`; objects `{ type: "sofa-2", place: "wall:N" }` and `{ type: "table-dining-4", place: "center" }` in `hall`, `{ type: "bed-single", place: "wall:W" }` in `bedroom`; interactables `{ id: "hall-switch", kind: "switch", room: "hall", x: <door.at + 1.2>, y: 1.2, z: <footprint.d/2 - 0.45>, group: "hall", prompt: "turn lights on" }` (just inside the south wall beside the exterior door), `{ id: "hall-desk", kind: "read", room: "hall", x: <table x>, y: 1.0, z: <table z>, dialogueKey: "main", readZone: "plaza", prompt: "read" }` and `{ id: "hall-sofa", kind: "sit", room: "hall", object: "sofa-2" }`; read `cottage.json` for the real coordinates and make the manifest pass `validateManifest` (the plan 020 schema may reject the optional fields `group`, `object`, `seatKind` (one of `sofa|bed|chair`), `readZone`, `hinge`, `variants`, the object field `text` (string) and the `place` forms `window:<id>` and `door:<id>`: if it does, extend `src/world/kit/schema.js` to accept them with tests in the new file `tests/unit/kit/schemaExtras.test.js`; do not edit frozen kit tests). Room field `wallMaterial` (a material name that is in `MATERIAL_NAMES`, default `plaster`; every wall face takes the material of the room it faces, the outside face of a perimeter wall keeps `style.wall`) belongs to plan 020: read `schema.js` and `shell.js` first; when it is missing, add it there and test it in `schemaExtras.test.js` (accepts a known name, rejects an unknown one with path `rooms[i].wallMaterial`) and in the new file `tests/unit/kit/wallMaterialShell.test.js` (a two-room manifest where room `b` has `wallMaterial: "brick"`: the partition faces looking into `b` use the brick material and the faces looking into `a` use plaster). `tests/fixtures/manifests/twoStoreyLift.json` = a copy of `twoStorey.json` plus `lifts: [{ id: "lift1", x, z, width: 2.0, depth: 2.0, rot: 0, floors: [0, 1] }]` placed inside the largest ground-floor room with a room of at least 2.4 x 2.4 m exactly above it on level 1 and the +z side (entrance) free of walls and stairs; check with `validateManifest`.',
          'Tests in `tests/unit/kit/parts.test.js` (stub context from `createHeadlessContext`): doors: hinge position and leaf yaw for ALL four wall letters with `left` and `right` hinge (8 expected values, interior door and exterior door), leaf size `width - 0.08` by `height - 0.05`, handle at y 1.0, a door id `<building>:<doorId>` gives collider `door:<building>:<doorId>` and an interactable of that id, `decorative` has no interactable and keeps its collider, `locked: true` door reports locked in `list()`; lights: each manifest light is registered with the prefixed id and world coordinates under a non-default placement (x 20, z -15, rot 30 degrees, y 2.0) and the room floor y added for a level 1 room; the bulb mesh is in the group; lifts: `floors` level indices are mapped to y, the `<building>:lift1-call-0` and `-btn-1` interactables exist, shaft mesh count, cabin follows `lift.y` after `lift.update` with fake time; `createHeadlessContext()` runs in Node and two calls give independent worlds. `tests/unit/kit/fixtures.test.js`: both fixture manifests validate; cottageFull has 2 lights, 3 object types, 3 interactables; twoStoreyLift has a lift.',
